REGENT OF GUNUNGKIDUL,
Considering : a. that all forms of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights and therefore their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;
b. that in addition to protection efforts, prevention, services, and empowerment are needed for women and children victims of violence;
c. that it is necessary to regulate the efforts as mentioned in letter b in the region;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas within the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 44);
3. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4844);
4. Government Regulation Number 32 of 1950 concerning the Determination of the Effective Date of Law Year 1950 Number 12, 13, 14 and 15 regarding the Establishment of Regency areas within the Province of Central Java, West Java and the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 59);
5. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence, State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604;
6. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
7. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 05 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
8. Special Regional Regulation of Yogyakarta Number 3 of 2012 concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of the Special Region Province of Yogyakarta Year 2012 Number 3);
